    Third-party data: TACO
    ----------------------
    Food composition values come from the Tabela Brasileira de Composicao de
    Alimentos (TACO), 4a edicao revisada e ampliada, Campinas: NEPA-UNICAMP,
    2011 -- https://nepa.unicamp.br/publicacoes/tabela-taco-pdf/

    (c) 2011 Nucleo de Estudos e Pesquisas em Alimentacao (NEPA), Universidade
    Estadual de Campinas (UNICAMP). Reproduced under the permission granted in
    the publication itself: "E permitida a reproducao total ou parcial do
    material, desde que seja citada a fonte" -- reproduction in whole or in
    part is permitted provided the source is cited.

    That condition travels with the data. If you copy the food data out of
    this repository, the MIT license does not release you from citing
    NEPA/UNICAMP, and it is not ours to relicense on their behalf.

    NEPA and UNICAMP published the table. They did not review, approve or
    endorse DietKit.

    Full terms, provenance and the rules DietKit holds itself to:
    docs/TACO-LICENSING.md

